      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "To evaluate the efficacy of gestrinone versus leuprolide acetate (LA) in improving pelvic pain in women with endometriosis and to compare their effects on bone mineral density and serum lipid profile."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Multicenter, double-blind, double-dummy, randomized clinical trial."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "Six academic departments specialized in the study of endometriosis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENT(S)",
          "content": "Fifty-five women with moderate or severe pelvic pain and laparoscopically diagnosed endometriosis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTION(S)",
          "content": "Six-month treatment with oral gestrinone (n = 27) or IM depot LA (n = 28) followed by 6-month follow-up."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE(S)",
          "content": "Variations in severity of dysmenorrhea, deep dyspareunia, and nonmenstrual pain as shown by a visual analog scale and a verbal rating scale, modifications in bone mineral content as shown by dual-roentgenogram absorptiometry, and variations in serum cholesterol subfractions and lipoprotein(a) concentrations."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULT(S)",
          "content": "Significant improvements were observed in all three symptoms considered in both treatment arms. Moderate or severe pain symptoms recurrence on both pain scales was observed in 2 of 17 (11.8%) patients given gestrinone compared with 9 of 17 (52.9%) of those given LA (odds ratio, 0.12; 95% confidence interval, 0.02 to 0.69). Lumbar bone mineral density increased slightly in the gestrinone group but decreased by 3% in the LA one. High-density-lipoprotein cholesterol fell by 25% and lipoprotein(a) decreased by approximately 40% in the gestrinone-treated women but did not vary in those receiving LA."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION(S)",
          "content": "Oral gestrinone is at least as effective as depot LA for pain relief in women with symptomatic endometriosis. A tendency to prolonged pain reduction was observed after gestrinone compared with LA treatment. Gestrinone does not negatively affect bone density but variations in serum lipids need further evaluation."
        }
      ]},
      "ArticleTitle": "Gestrinone versus a gonadotropin-releasing hormone agonist for the treatment of pelvic pain associated with endometriosis: a multicenter, randomized, double-blind study. Gestrinone Italian Study Group.",
